# <title>

Use this concise contract for normal interactive work. Do not use it for a direct one-shot edit
that needs no coordination, or for unattended/genuinely independent multi-slice work; those use the protected-plan
workflow in `shared/planning-recipe.md`.

This document records intent and evidence. It has no lifecycle status and cannot authorize work.
Amend it only while refining the work; when the result is recorded, freeze it as the durable
contract for this change.

## Outcome and scope

- **Observable outcome:** <one externally checkable result>
- **Task class:** <behavioral_code | docs_config | refactor | research_design>
- **Writable paths:** <specific files or directories>
- **Protected paths:** <tests, policies, generated artifacts, or other paths that must not change>
- **Baseline:** <the safe scoped command and its result, or why it was not practical to run>

## Delivery plan and user review

For coordinated multi-step work, keep one parent delivery objective and complete this table before
implementation. A direct one-shot edit may record why this plan and review are not needed. This
section records conversational intent only; it is not lifecycle state or a protected approval
record.

- **Parent delivery objective:** <end-to-end result for the user>
- **Review exception, if any:** <direct one-shot edit or explicit user waiver>

| Phase | Deliverable and evidence | Gate / review outcome |
|---|---|---|
| Context and intent | <active outcome or decision packet> | <resolved / decision needed> |
| Plan and user review | <scope, non-goals, alternatives, acceptance, risks> | <approved / revise / pause / cancel> |
| Implementation and integration | <bounded slices and integration evidence> | <proceed / rework / stop-replan> |
| Verification and validation | <criteria proof and user-need observation> | <accepted / rework> |
| Delivery and closure | <handoff, authorized publication, residual risks, evidence> | <complete / follow-up> |

Do not implement until the user has reviewed this plan, unless the review exception above applies.
A phase or slice can enable the next phase but cannot complete the parent delivery objective.

## Completion criteria

Use **Given** only for material starting conditions, **When** for the completed user action or
state transition, and **Then** for independently observable results. Every `Then` criterion is
mandatory; write the expected output, access decision, file, response, or other concrete signal,
not “works correctly.”

**Given:**

- <material starting condition>

**When:**

- <completed action or state transition>

**Then all of the following are true:**

- <observable success criterion>
- <observable edge case, authorization, compatibility, or regression criterion>
- <automated or manual proof criterion, if it is itself the required result>

## Acceptance and regression checks

| Purpose | Exact command | Expected signal |
|---|---|---|
| Acceptance | `<argv or shell command>` | <exit code and relevant pass text/value> |
| Regression / inherited check | `<command>` | <expected result> |

The checker reruns these commands independently when practical. Do not weaken, skip, or edit a
check to obtain green. When a command cannot establish a `Then` criterion, record the precise
manual observation required to establish it.

## Alternatives considered

| Alternative | Why rejected |
|---|---|
| <credible option> | <why it is less suitable here> |

Record the credible alternatives actually considered; do not invent a quota of artificial options.

## Escalate instead of guessing when

- acceptance, scope, or a material product decision is unclear;
- the baseline is unexpectedly red;
- the work becomes unattended, genuinely independent multi-slice, irreversible, external, or higher risk; or
- repeated verification is not making progress.

Time and cost are planning estimates unless the host can measure and enforce them.

